# Vyayamy — Project Conventions

## Architecture

Vyayamy is a **mobile-only, local-first** strength-training journal built with Expo + React Native. SQLite on the device is the source of truth during a session; Supabase is a durable mirror reached only by the sync engine. Do not introduce API servers, ORMs, middleware, or server-side rendering. The UI must never block on the network.

Legacy `legacy-web/` is a frozen pre-pivot PWA. Do not import from it and do not update it.

## Stack Guardrails

Do NOT replace, remove, or migrate away from any of the following without explicit approval and a documented reason:

- **Expo SDK 51**, **React Native 0.74**, **React 18** (no DOM, no web APIs)
- **TypeScript** with `strict: true`
- **Expo Router** (file-based, typed routes) for navigation
- **`expo-sqlite`** as the local source of truth
- **Supabase JS client** talking directly to PostgREST + GoTrue — reached **only** from `src/sync/**` and `src/auth/**`
- **TanStack React Query 5** for all server state (reads SQLite, not HTTP)
- **`StyleSheet.create`** + tokens from `src/ui/theme.ts` — no CSS files, no CSS-in-JS
- **`react-native-svg`** for charts
- **`expo-haptics`**, **`expo-notifications`** for feedback and background rest cues
- **`@sentry/react-native`** for error reporting (gated by `EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN`)
- **Jest + `ts-jest`** with `better-sqlite3` mocking `expo-sqlite`

Do not add state management libraries (Redux, Zustand, Jotai, etc.). UI state uses `useState`/`useReducer`; server state belongs in React Query.

Do not add Recharts or `victory-native` (React version conflict). Charts are in-house SVG.

## Directory Structure

```
app/                          Expo Router routes (file-based)
  _layout.tsx                 Root stack + providers + db init + sync engine
  (tabs)/                     Bottom tabs (today, history, progress, profile)
  login.tsx, workout/*,       Stack screens
  history/[id].tsx, profile/plan/*

src/
  auth/                       Supabase client, AuthProvider, useAuth
  components/                 Shared presentational components
  core/                       Pure domain logic (PR detection, format, sync helpers)
  db/                         SQLite schema, client, enqueueMutation, uuid, types, mocks
  lib/                        Cross-cutting services (errorReporting, restNotifications)
  native/health/              HealthKit + Health Connect adapter interface
  queries/                    React Query hooks reading SQLite, one file per domain
  screens/                    Large screens imported by app/ routes
  sync/                       engine.ts, push.ts, pull.ts, state.ts
  ui/                         theme.ts, primitives, charts, error boundary
  __tests__/                  Integration tests

supabase/
  migrations/                 Numbered SQL migrations
  seed.sql                    Global exercise library
```

Preserve this layout. New features fit into the existing directories. Do not restructure, flatten, or introduce barrel files (`index.ts` re-exports).

## File Naming

| Kind                | Convention  | Example                    |
| ------------------- | ----------- | -------------------------- |
| Screens/components  | PascalCase  | `ExerciseBlock.tsx`        |
| Route files         | lowercase   | `today.tsx`, `[id].tsx`    |
| Query modules       | camelCase   | `workouts.ts`, `sets.ts`   |
| Lib/utility files   | camelCase   | `errorReporting.ts`        |
| Type files          | camelCase   | `types.ts`                 |

## Import Order

1. React / React hooks
2. React Native primitives (`View`, `Text`, `Pressable`, ...)
3. Third-party packages (Expo, TanStack Query, Supabase, Sentry, ...)
4. Internal modules via `@/` alias (`@/db`, `@/sync`, `@/ui`, ...)
5. Type-only imports use `import type { ... }`

No CSS imports — styles are co-located in the component file as `StyleSheet.create`.

## Provider Tree (do not reorder)

Defined in `app/_layout.tsx`:

```
ErrorBoundary → SafeAreaProvider → QueryClientProvider → AuthProvider → ToastProvider → <Stack>
```

`RootLayout` must `initDb()` before rendering the Stack and `startSyncEngine(queryClient)` on mount.

## Cross-cutting Rules

- UI code must not call `supabase.from(...)`. Only `src/sync/push.ts` and `src/sync/pull.ts` do. Auth code in `src/auth/supabase.ts` is the only other place that touches the Supabase client.
- Every read query must filter `deleted_at IS NULL`. Tombstones are for the sync engine.
- Every mutation must go through `enqueueMutation` in `src/db/mutations.ts`.
- New synced tables must be added to `SYNCED_TABLES` in `src/db/schema.ts` AND have `updated_at` + `deleted_at` in their Postgres migration.
